agent-hint-no-daemon = easyshot isn't running. Start it with `systemctl --user start easyshot`.
agent-hint-access-off = Agent access is off. Turn it on in Settings › Agents, or run `easyshot agent enable`.
agent-hint-access-denied = You didn't allow this request, so nothing was done.
agent-hint-change-cancelled = You cancelled the change in the confirmation, so it was not made.
agent-hint-outside-scope = That is outside what agents may capture. Allow it in Settings › Agents, or run `easyshot agent config set`.
agent-hint-capture-busy = You're in the middle of a capture. Finish it or press Esc, and try again.
agent-hint-recording-busy = A recording is already running. Stop it, then try again.
agent-hint-tesseract-missing = Reading text needs Tesseract. Install it with `sudo pacman -S tesseract tesseract-data-eng`.
agent-hint-no-recorder = No screen recorder is installed. Install gpu-screen-recorder or wf-recorder, for example `sudo pacman -S wf-recorder`.
agent-hint-window-unreachable = easyshot couldn’t switch to { $window }. Ask the user to switch to its workspace, or pick a window that is on screen.
agent-hint-ffmpeg-missing = Exporting needs ffmpeg. Install it with `sudo pacman -S ffmpeg`.
agent-hint-no-window = No open window is called "{ $query }". Open windows: { $windows }.
agent-hint-no-window-none = No open window is called "{ $query }", and no windows are open.
agent-hint-window-ambiguous = More than one window matches "{ $query }": { $windows }. Say which one you mean.
agent-hint-no-output = No monitor is called "{ $query }". Monitors: { $outputs }.
agent-hint-no-audio-device = The sound device "{ $device }" wasn't found. Pick another in Settings › Recording, or turn the sound off.
agent-hint-no-audio-device-default = The microphone or sound device wasn't found. Pick another in Settings › Recording, or turn the sound off.
agent-hint-area-off-monitor = The area to record isn't on any monitor. Choose an area inside one monitor.
agent-hint-file-missing = There is no file at { $path }. Check the path and try again.
agent-hint-not-an-image = { $path } isn't an image easyshot can read. Use a PNG or JPEG file.

doctor-cap-layer-shell = Overlays on screen
doctor-cap-layer-shell-missing = the selection and the deck cannot draw over your screen
doctor-cap-capture-output = Capture a screen
doctor-cap-capture-output-missing = you cannot capture a whole screen or a region
doctor-cap-capture-window = Capture a window
doctor-cap-capture-window-missing = you cannot capture a single window
doctor-cap-window-list = List windows
doctor-cap-window-list-missing = you cannot pick a window by pointing at it
doctor-cap-window-geometry = Window positions
doctor-cap-window-geometry-missing = windows cannot be outlined or snapped to
doctor-cap-clipboard-no-focus = Copy without focus
doctor-cap-clipboard-no-focus-missing = copying may fail unless an easyshot window has focus
doctor-cap-tray = Tray icon
doctor-cap-tray-missing = there is no tray icon
doctor-cap-notify-actions = Notification buttons
doctor-cap-notify-actions-missing = notifications have no buttons
doctor-cap-portal-shortcuts = Shortcuts through the portal
doctor-cap-portal-shortcuts-missing = easyshot cannot register keys through the desktop portal
doctor-cap-shortcut-triggers = Shortcut keys
doctor-cap-shortcut-triggers-missing = easyshot cannot read which keys you have set
doctor-cap-pointer-global = Pointer position
doctor-cap-pointer-global-missing = easyshot cannot tell where the pointer is on screen
doctor-cap-virtual-input = Scrolling for you
doctor-cap-virtual-input-missing = scroll capture cannot scroll the page itself
doctor-cap-recorder = Screen recording
doctor-cap-recorder-missing = you cannot record the screen
doctor-cap-ocr = Read text
doctor-cap-ocr-missing = you cannot read text from a capture
doctor-cap-bind-check = Shortcut check
doctor-cap-bind-check-missing = easyshot cannot tell whether your keys are bound
doctor-cap-file-picker = File dialogs
doctor-cap-file-picker-missing = open and save use easyshot's own dialog
doctor-cap-appearance = Light and dark mode
doctor-cap-appearance-missing = easyshot does not follow your light or dark setting
doctor-cap-cursor-stream = Cursor in recordings
doctor-cap-cursor-stream-missing = recordings cannot show the pointer
doctor-cap-focus-window = Switch to a window
doctor-cap-focus-window-missing = a window on another workspace cannot be recorded
doctor-cap-record-window = Record a window by itself
doctor-cap-record-window-missing = window recordings record the window's area on screen
doctor-daemon-down = The daemon is not running; this is a { $source } probe.
doctor-compositor = Compositor:
doctor-heading-works = What works
doctor-heading-providers = Chosen providers
doctor-heading-missing = Missing tools
doctor-heading-errors = Errors
doctor-forced = (forced: { $forced })
doctor-provider-none = none
doctor-install-package = install the package { $package }
doctor-raw-hint = Run `easyshot doctor --raw` for the full report.
doctor-input-granted = can read the keyboard and mouse
doctor-input-denied = cannot read the keyboard and mouse
doctor-input-group-pending = cannot read the keyboard and mouse yet (added to the group, log out and in)
doctor-input-absent = not in this build
doctor-input = Clicks and keys in recordings: { $state }
doctor-input-fix = Fix: { $fix }
doctor-input-records = Records { $what }
doctor-config = Settings file: { $path } ({ $status }{ $detail })
cli-line = easyshot: { $text }
cli-handled-by-main = handled by main, not sent
cli-daemon-not-running = the daemon is not running. Start it with `easyshot daemon` or `systemctl --user start easyshot.service`.
cli-daemon-gone = the daemon went away before it finished.
cli-session-bus = cannot talk to the session bus: { $error }
cli-cancelled = cancelled
cli-share-not-set-up = sharing is not set up yet. Open Settings › Sharing to choose where your shares go, then run this again.
cli-sharing = preparing and uploading, this can take a while
cli-probe-failed = the standalone probe failed: { $error }
cli-wrote = wrote { $path }
cli-no-gui = this build has no GUI; rebuild with the `gui` feature to run the daemon
